WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:07.350
Every time we talk about how X or Y scenario
is likely to go forward during what is hopefully

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.730
the last 15 months of Donald Trump's presidency.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:16.180
Those analyses assume that Republicans are
not going to turn on Donald Trump, that in

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.930
the end, Republican senators would not vote
to impeach Donald Trump, that Trump's Republican

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.500
cabinet would not use the 25th amendment to
try to remove Trump from power.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.030
Those are the assumptions that we're operating
under.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:32.820
However, former Trump white house communications
director, I think he lasted 10 days.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.429
Anthony Scaramucci has a different perspective.

00:00:35.429 --> 00:00:41.620
He now says that 20 or more Republicans are
set to turn on Donald Trump.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.730
This is Scaramucci effectively predicting
a sort of Nixon like scenario from the 1970s

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.631
you might remember Republicans, a Weddington
Nixon in the 70s and the wake of in the, in

00:00:50.631 --> 00:00:57.179
the midst of the Watergate fiasco and said,
listen, we don't want to impeach you, but

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:01.479
we're going to have to if it comes to a vote,
so why don't you resign?

00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:07.000
And that's exactly what Richard Nixon did
check out Scaramucci on CNN making the case.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.210
Well, you know, he obviously knows a lot more
facts about the case are going to unfold over

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.979
the next, you know, two to six weeks, Don.

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:19.322
And so I think that's got him rattled and
I think he's, he's also looking at the future.

00:01:19.322 --> 00:01:24.579
The future does not look good for him because
as more facts unfold about Syria, as more

00:01:24.579 --> 00:01:29.380
facts unfold about the people that have been
arrested recently and the conjoint of all

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.340
those issues over there, uh, it's going to
be devastating for the president and what

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.560
will ultimately happen, which I predicted
on CNN air two months ago.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.750
Uh, the full blown meltdown we're experiencing
speaker Pelosi described it today, but will

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.899
eventually will eventually happen, is the
criminal activity will be so great that the

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:51.719
GOP, and there'll be 20 plus senators will
say, okay, I can't take this anymore.

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:56.770
Reminiscent of what Howard Baker and, uh,
Barry Goldwater did in the 70s and called

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:59.189
Richard Nixon and said, look, no Moss, you
gotta go.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:01.439
And so that, that will eventually happen.

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:03.869
And that's the reason why he's pressurized.

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:09.840
But I really wish the white house press would
just ask him what was in it for him personally.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.190
So this is just one guy, right?

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.420
I mean, this is just Anthony Scaramucci.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.500
You never want to put too much stock into
what any one person says.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:21.470
But this is a narrative that has been floating
around for awhile and the idea is actually

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.730
deeper than 20 Republicans will turn on Trump.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:29.500
The real idea is a whole bunch of Republicans
have already turned on Trump in their minds

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.610
internally.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:35.470
The question is that they are balancing their
own political futures with doing what they

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.580
believe is right, which is turning on Donald
Trump.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.140
Now, this isn't a great moral realization
about Republicans.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.380
Republicans who support Trump are immoral
and indifferent to supporting so-called conservative

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.380
values.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.950
That's bad enough.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:55.311
Republicans who privately don't support Trump
but continue to support them publicly, they

00:02:55.311 --> 00:02:56.730
are also terrible.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:02.100
They're merely choosing political expediency
in calculation for the benefit of their careers

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.290
over what they actually believe would be good
for the country, which is pretty damn bad

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.540
in a different way.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.260
So when we hear Scaramucci say it, he may
know what he's talking about.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.260
He may not.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.150
It'll be interesting to see if and when it
happens, but to the extent that this is an

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:21.660
existing narrative that we've been following,
we just need to watch the polls.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.080
Support for impeachment and removal has been
climbing.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:30.470
If we believe that there are at least some
disgruntled Republican senators out of the

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:36.720
53 uh, that are currently in the Senate and
they're waiting around for public support

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.590
to be high enough that the risk to their careers
is diminished.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.510
If they come out and say, it is time to remove
Donald Trump, we're pretty damn close to getting

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.510
there.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:52.430
We have a support for impeachment and removal
hitting and surpassing 50% in a hyperpolarized,

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.240
modern status quo of American politics.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:04:02.130
You're not going to get that much more before
it becomes tantamount to major support for

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.060
removing the president of the United States
from office.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:10.070
And what we know is that these Republican
senators are all about just putting their

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:15.920
finger to the wind, trying to end up on the
right side of public opinion, conservative

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.000
so-called values.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.230
Be damned so we don't even have to put any
special stock in what Anthony Scaramucci is

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:23.420
saying here.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.300
This has been a possibility for awhile.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.720
We've been considering it for about a year
and a half and we'll follow it.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:35.310
There is a timing issue though as we are now
only um, 12 and a half months from the 2020

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:40.280
election, which is if Republicans are going
to turn on Trump, they sort of need to do

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.952
it pretty soon before it's going to be too
little too late.

